h3. Event Key

The event key is {{search_eta_delta}}. It’s already created on both live and prelive admins, under the name of _Search ETA Delta_.

----

h3. Rules

{{user_id}} and {{city_id}} are then only parameters send, so the rules can be based on either.

----

h3. Parameters

The parameters JSON for the tests have the following schema:

{noformat}{
  "search_eta_delta_in_minutes": 10,
  "excluded_provider_ids": [
    <id_mc_donalds>, <id_bolt_market>
  ],
  "search_eta_minimum_in_minutes": 20
}{noformat}

* only {{search_eta_delta_in_minutes}} is required
* {{search_eta_delta_in_minutes}} can be either negative or positive (or zero if you want it to be disabled)
* default value for {{search_eta_minimum_in_minutes}} is currently 10 minutes
* expected behaviour is that if {{search_eta_minimum_in_minutes}} is bigger than {{search_eta_delta_in_minutes}} + real_search_eta_in_minutes, then delta will not be added, so it will keep the value of real_search_eta_in_minutes (even if this value is by itself lower than {{search_eta_minimum_in_minutes}}); this behaviour is relevant only for negative delta values, as the delta is by default added to real_search_eta_in_minutes.


----

h3. Example parameters JSON

This will do nothing (Control group):

{noformat}{
  "search_eta_delta_in_minutes": 0
}{noformat}


This will reduce all search ETAs by 15 minutes (if the search ETA - 15 is >= 10):

{code:json}{
  "search_eta_delta_in_minutes": -15
}{code}



This will add 15 minutes to all search ETAs, excepting for the provider with id 1: 

{noformat}{
  "search_eta_delta_in_minutes": 10,
  "excluded_provider_ids": [
    1
  ],
}{noformat}


This will reduce all search ETAs by 15 minutes (if the search ETA - 15 is >= to 60):

{noformat}{
  "search_eta_delta_in_minutes": -15,
  "search_eta_minimum_in_minutes": 60
}{noformat}

